column34:
{color:#000000}*Summary:*{color}

{color:#000000}The ESTAP {color}{color:#000000}is comprised of the ESTAP controller and ESTAP Graphical User Interface (GUI). The ESTAP GUI is what the operator uses to control the movement of the tube 9 and tube 10 hatches{color}. It is responsible for providing the visuals needed to for operators to conduct SSW mission operations. The ESTAP GUI allows operators to view the live status of the External Stowage Tray System (ESTS). It also allows operators to move the tray and override sensor values. The purpose of this milestone is to document the design for all the units of ESTAP GUI as well as initial implementation and testing for all units.

This milestone specifically encompasses all units comprising the Manual Mode Page. {color:#172b4d}NOTE:  Design and implementation is based on the most recently available and reviewed GUI mockups from the EST GUI Penpot project. Visual mockups are subject to change and we expect to identity edge cases as we produce software designs and begin implementation.{color}

{color:#ff0000}Each page that is displayed will be considered a unit. We will need sub-unit pages to capture specific/key variations of a given unit page. Should be re-evaluated before tasks are added into the PI.{color}

*Project Impact:*
{color:#000000}What Problem Does this Solve{color}
 * {color:#000000}Produces design documentation for common and ESTAP GUI code used in the ESTAP CSCI.{color}
 * {color:#000000}Provides clarity for safety teams, stakeholders and developers{color}
 * Work towards engineering and tactical GUI development; tested implementation for the ESTAP GUI Manual Mode Page

{color:#000000}How does this fit into the larger project{color}
 * {color:#000000}This documentation will be included in the ESTAP SDD. {color}
 * This enables us to start developing our engineering GUIs. 

{color:#000000}*Implementation Overview:*{color}
{color:#000000}High Level Overview{color}
 * {color:#000000}The ESTAP design pages will document the design of the Tube 10 Control Page and all the React Components within.{color}
 ** {color:#000000}Tray Animation Area{color}

 * 
 ** 
 *** {color:#000000}TCS tube bottom hatches {color}
 *** {color:#000000}the ROV{color}
 *** {color:#000000}the tray {color}
 ** {color:#000000}Sensor Data Area - left hand side{color}
 ** {color:#000000}Tray Package Configuration  - bottom middle{color}
 ** {color:#000000}Tray Commands - bottom right  {color}
 ** {color:#000000}Tray Two state commands - top right {color}
 *** {color:#000000}LL Synchronous{color}
 *** {color:#000000}LL Asynchronous{color}
 *** {color:#000000}Fore/Aft{color}
 *** {color:#000000}Mode of Operations{color}

{color:#000000}Key Components/Docs{color}
